//
// Veld & Carrying Capacity — Phase 6 permit-document Storage rules
// (MERGE FRAGMENT).
//
// THIS FILE IS NOT A COMPLETE RULESET. It must NOT replace `storage.rules`.
// It is the block to paste INTO the live `storage.rules`, inside
// `service firebase.storage { match /b/{bucket}/o { ... } }`, immediately
// ABOVE the existing default-deny catch-all:
//
//     match /{allPaths=**} {
//       allow read, write: if false;
//     }
//
// That catch-all must remain the LAST block.
//
// ── What it protects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Permit documents uploaded by `VeldCarryPermitFormScreen` via
// `ImageService.uploadDocument` land at:
//
//   veld_permits/{outfitterUid}/{farmId}/{permitId}/{fileName}
//
// See `VeldCarryPermitFormScreen.permitStoragePath` — that builder is the
// authoritative contract and the path segments are stripped of `/` so a
// crafted file name cannot escape its permit folder.
//
// ── Access model ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   • OWNER READ/WRITE ONLY. The second path segment is the outfitter's uid,
//     so `request.auth.uid == outfitterUid` is a single, non-spoofable check
//     that needs no document read.
//   • NO public read. A permit document is regulatory paperwork (permit
//     numbers, issuing authorities) and must never be world-readable.
//   • NO hunter read. The hunter veld view deliberately renders permit TYPE +
//     EXPIRY + STATUS only and never links the file — the hunter must not be
//     able to fetch it even with the URL. Granting a hunter read here would
//     break that contract, so there is deliberately no hunter clause.
//   • NO admin bypass. Add `|| isAdmin()` only if Llewellyn approves it
//     explicitly at go-live (matches the Firestore fragment's posture).
//
// ── Validation performed on this file ────────────────────────────────────
//   • braces balanced, parens balanced.
//   • no unconditional read grant anywhere.
//   • every path below matches `permitStoragePath` exactly.
//
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// [MERGE] permit documents — owner read/write only
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    match /veld_permits/{outfitterUid}/{farmId}/{permitId}/{fileName} {
      // The owning outfitter reads and writes their own permit documents.
      // `request.auth != null` is implied by the uid comparison, but it is
      // stated explicitly so an unauthenticated request can never satisfy the
      // clause by comparing null to a path segment.
      allow read: if request.auth != null
        && request.auth.uid == outfitterUid;
      allow write: if request.auth != null
        && request.auth.uid == outfitterUid;
    }

